>
  
  <script type="application/json" data-target="react-app.embeddedData">{"payload":{"preloaded_records":{},"structured_data":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","headline":"index-url extra-index-url install priority order","articleBody":"This is totally related to #5045, but I can not comment on it.\r\n\r\nFor me this should be re-opened, because it's a security issue.\r\n\r\nI provide the package `xxx` to the private repository `my-company.com`. Then I gives installation instructions to collaborators, configure CI to install this package, etc.\r\n\r\nThe problem is if someone add a package with the same name on pypi.org, then users and CI will get this package instead of mine, which is bad: and I want to be sure that the installation will not change.\r\n\r\nIt's not about naming package: if I name my packe `my_company.xxx`, a malicious user could chose the exact same name and publish it to pypi, letting my collaborators installing a malware instead of my package.","author":{"url":"https://github.com/lypwig","@type":"Person","name":"lypwig"},"datePublished":"2020-07-21T07:31:15.000Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"https://schema.org/CommentAction","userInteractionCount":132},"url":"https://github.com/8606/pip/issues/8606"},"best_match_sort_enabled":false,"issue_search_type":"ISSUE_HYBRID","preloadedQueries":[{"queryId":"7b8046626ec35743f2ca3b2c0ac4749e","queryName":"IssueViewerViewQuery","variables":{"count":15,"number":8606,"owner":"pypa","repo":"pip"},"result":{"data":{"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxNDQ2NDY3","isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","userNameDisplayConfiguration":"HANDLE","id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjY0NzAyNQ=="},"issue":{"id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2NjI2OTQ5NTA=","number":8606,"viewerCanUpdateMetadata":false,"repository":{"id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxNDQ2NDY3","databaseId":1446467,"name":"pip","isArchived":false,"nameWithOwner":"pypa/pip","viewerCanInteract":false,"viewerInteractionLimitReasonHTML":"","slashCommandsEnabled":false,"visibility":"PUBLIC","viewerCanPush":false,"owner":{"__typename":"Organization","login":"pypa","id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjY0NzAyNQ==","url":"https://github.com/pypa","databaseId":647025,"issueFields":{"totalCount":0},"pinnedIssueFields":{"nodes":[]}},"isPrivate":false,"isWritable":true,"isOwnerEnterpriseManaged":false,"viewerCanPinIssues":false,"isCopilotAgentEnabled":null,"issueTypes":{"edges":[]},"pinnedIssues":{"totalCount":1},"viewerIssueCreationPermissions":{"triageable":false}},"updatedAt":"2026-04-16T17:24:38Z","titleHTML":"index-url extra-index-url install priority order","url":"https://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/8606","viewerCanUpdateNext":false,"issueType":null,"duplicateOf":null,"linkedPullRequests":{"nodes":[]},"agentAssignments":[],"closedByPullRequestsReferences":{"nodes":[]},"labels":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"MQ"},"edges":[{"node":{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDc1MDYyMjU0","color":"0052cc","name":"C: finder","nameHTML":"C: finder","description":"PackageFinder and index related code","url":"https://github.com/pypa/pip/labels/C%3A%20finder","archivedAt":null}}]},"milestone":null,"assignedActors":{"nodes":[]},"locked":false,"viewerCanComment":false,"databaseId":662694950,"state":"OPEN","stateReason":null,"title":"index-url extra-index-url install priority order","createdAt":"2020-07-21T07:31:15Z","viewerDidAuthor":false,"author":{"avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1665542?u=7c07b93b654e71c9d371f798a236eabca9b3eeec\u0026v=4","login":"lypwig","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjU1NDI=","profileUrl":"https://github.com/lypwig","name":null,"__typename":"User"},"body":"This is totally related to #5045, but I can not comment on it.\r\n\r\nFor me this should be re-opened, because it's a security issue.\r\n\r\nI provide the package `xxx` to the private repository `my-company.com`. Then I gives installation instructions to collaborators, configure CI to install this package, etc.\r\n\r\nThe problem is if someone add a package with the same name on pypi.org, then users and CI will get this package instead of mine, which is bad: and I want to be sure that the installation will not change.\r\n\r\nIt's not about naming package: if I name my packe `my_company.xxx`, a malicious user could chose the exact same name and publish it to pypi, letting my collaborators installing a malware instead of my package.","bodyHTML":"\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis is totally related to \u003ca class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"301252726\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/5045\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/pypa/pip/issues/5045/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/5045\"\u003e#5045\u003c/a\u003e, but I can not comment on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eFor me this should be re-opened, because it's a security issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eI provide the package \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003exxx\u003c/code\u003e to the private repository \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003emy-company.com\u003c/code\u003e. Then I gives installation instructions to collaborators, configure CI to install this package, etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe problem is if someone add a package with the same name on pypi.org, then users and CI will get this package instead of mine, which is bad: and I want to be sure that the installation will not change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIt's not about naming package: if I name my packe \u003ccode class=\"notranslate\"\u003emy_company.xxx\u003c/code\u003e, a malicious user could chose the exact same name and publish it to pypi, letting my collaborators installing a malware instead of my package.\u003c/p\u003e","bodyVersion":"dcaecafc3fa417aae351d14255cdd83f2f7748d69480451a4cb10f0d9da2a938","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP"